<!--ID=FCB40C2B-1F9F-4C26-B1A1-CF8E67BE07D1;Version=1|{"Files":{}}-->
<!--ID=5B95B1CC-2C7B-494F-B746-CF22A0E779B7;Version=1|{"Locales":{"en-US":{"AutoApplyCustomLexiconFiles":[{}]},"en-GB":{"AutoApplyCustomLexiconFiles":[{}]}}}-->
<speak xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2001/10/synthesis"
       xmlns:mstts="http://www.w3.org/2001/mstts"
       xmlns:emo="http://www.w3.org/2009/10/emotionml"
       version="1.0"
       xml:lang="en-GB">
  <voice name="en-GB-OllieMultilingualNeural">
    <prosody rate="-10.75%" pitch="-2.60%">
      Jacob was left alone in the dark beside the Jabbok.<break time="500ms"/>
      The water moved quietly over the stones.<break time="500ms"/>
      The night was still.<break time="1800ms"/>

      And then a man wrestled with him.<break time="500ms"/>
      We are not told where the man came from.<break time="500ms"/>
      We are not told what words were spoken first.<break time="1000ms"/>
      Only that they struggled together until the breaking of the day.<break time="1800ms"/>

      Through the long hours of darkness, Jacob held on.<break time="500ms"/>
      He would not release his grip.<break time="500ms"/>
      He would not give in.<break time="1800ms"/>

      When the man saw that he did not prevail against Jacob, he touched the socket of his hip.<break time="500ms"/>
      And Jacob's hip was put out of joint as they wrestled.<break time="1800ms"/>

      Still Jacob held on.<break time="500ms"/>
      Even broken, he would not let go.<break time="1000ms"/>
      The man said, Let me go, for the day has broken.<break time="1800ms"/>

      But Jacob said, I will not let you go unless you bless me.<break time="1000ms"/>
      The man said, What is your name?<break time="500ms"/>
      He answered, Jacob.<break time="1800ms"/>

      Then the man said, Your name shall no longer be called Jacob, but Israel.<break time="500ms"/>
      For you have striven with God and with men, and have prevailed.<break time="1800ms"/>

      Jacob asked, Please tell me your name.<break time="500ms"/>
      But the man said, Why is it that you ask my name?<break time="1000ms"/>
      And there he blessed him.<break time="1800ms"/>

      Something changed in the dark that night.<break time="500ms"/>
      Jacob came as one man and would leave as another.<break time="1000ms"/>
      You can rest.<break time="3800ms"/>
    </prosody>
  </voice>
</speak>
